.TH AUDITGET 1
.SH NAME
auditget \- fetch and verify an audit-record payload
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B auditget
[
.B -a
.I addr
] [
.B -s
.I sha256
]
.I score
.SH DESCRIPTION
A payload-bearing audit record (see
.IR auditprov (2))
carries
.B content=
and
.B sha256=
fields.
.I Auditget
fetches the payload named by
.I score
from the provenance content store and streams it to standard output.
The venti fetch itself verifies every block against its score; with
.B -s
the payload is additionally checked against the given SHA-256 \(em the
hash the audit chain sealed \(em and the command fails on mismatch.
.PP
.B -a
names the content store; the default is the
.B auditventi
environment variable, then
.BR tcp!127.0.0.1!17034 .
.SH EXAMPLE
Fetch and verify the payload of a chain record:
.EX
	; grep 'veltro task' /mnt/audit/chain
	1042 ... veltro task agent=7 content=5d1f\fI...\fP sha256=29da\fI...\fP size=41
	; auditget -s 29da\fI...\fP 5d1f\fI...\fP
.EE
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/auditget.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR auditprov (2),
.IR auditfs (4),
.IR ventisrv (8)
